### Configuration Requirements

**Environment Variables:**
```bash
# Provider Selection
LLM_PROVIDER=AZURE_OPENAI
EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=AZURE_OPENAI

# Azure OpenAI Configuration
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource.cognitiveservices.azure.com/
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2025-01-01-preview

# Deployment Names (created in Azure Portal)
AZURE_OPENAI_CHAT_DEPLOYMENT=o4-mini
AZURE_OPENAI_EMBEDDING_DEPLOYMENT=text-embedding-ada-002
```

### Authentication Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant App as RAG Application
    participant Config as Config Manager
    participant Azure as Azure OpenAI
    participant Entra as Microsoft Entra ID
    participant KeyVault as Azure Key Vault

    Note over App,Config: Method 1: API Key (Development)
    App->>Config: Load AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY
    App->>Azure: Request with x-api-key header
    Azure-->>App: Response

    Note over App,KeyVault: Method 2: Entra ID (Production)
    App->>Entra: Request access token<br/>(ClientCredential or ManagedIdentity)
    Entra-->>App: JWT Bearer token
    App->>Azure: Request with Authorization: Bearer {token}
    Azure->>Entra: Validate token & check RBAC
    Entra-->>Azure: Token valid, user has permissions
    Azure-->>App: Response
    
    Note over App,KeyVault: Optional: Key Vault Integration
    App->>Entra: Get token for Key Vault
    Entra-->>App: Key Vault token
    App->>KeyVault: Retrieve AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY
    KeyVault-->>App: API key (encrypted in transit)
```

### Key Benefits

| Category | Benefit | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| **Security** | Private Endpoints | VNet integration, no public internet exposure |
| | Entra ID Authentication | Role-based access control (RBAC) |
| | Data Residency | Data stays in your chosen Azure region |
| | No Training | Your data is never used for model training |
| **Compliance** | Certifications | SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA, GDPR |
| | Audit Logs | Complete audit trail in Azure Monitor |
| | Data Governance | Control over data location and access |
| **Cost** | Predictable Pricing | Reserved capacity and quotas |
| | Quota Management | Set limits per deployment |
| | Cost Analysis | Azure Cost Management integration |
| **Reliability** | SLA | 99.9% uptime guarantee |
| | Regional Failover | Multi-region deployment support |
| | Monitoring | Azure Monitor and Application Insights |

### Migration Guide

**From OpenAI to Azure OpenAI:**

1. **Create Azure OpenAI Resource**
   - Azure Portal → Create Resource → Azure OpenAI
   - Select region (consider data residency)
   - Choose pricing tier

2. **Deploy Models**
   - Create chat model deployment (e.g., gpt-4o, o4-mini)
   - Create embedding deployment (text-embedding-ada-002)
   - Note deployment names (used in config)

3. **Update Configuration**
   ```bash
   # Change from
   LLM_PROVIDER=OPENAI
   EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=OPENAI
   
   # To
   LLM_PROVIDER=AZURE_OPENAI
   EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=AZURE_OPENAI
   ```

4. **Add Azure Variables**
   - Set AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT
   - Set AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY
   - Set deployment names

5. **Re-ingest Documents** (if switching embedding provider)
   - Embedding dimensions must match
   - OpenAI and Azure OpenAI both use 1536 dims (compatible)
   - Only re-ingest if switching to/from LOCAL embeddings

6. **Restart Application**
   - Backend will automatically detect Azure configuration
   - No code changes required

### RBAC Roles

| Role | Permissions | Use Case |
|------|-------------|----------|
| **Cognitive Services OpenAI User** | Read + Execute | Application runtime identity |
| **Cognitive Services OpenAI Contributor** | Read + Write + Execute | DevOps, deployment management |
| **Cognitive Services User** | Limited read access | Monitoring only |

